---
description: Spec-driven Dostigus — read SPEC/ADRs, keep glossary stable
alwaysApply: true
---

Before writing code, read `docs/SPEC.md` and `docs/adr/README.md` (next ADR number = max + 1; headings Decision, Context, Consequences, Alternatives). Use only CONTEXT.md terms (Host not Host shell; MCP surface not MCP contract as the runtime name; Bot ≠ Module package; Builder not “cloud agent”). Do not invent synonyms. Docs and glossary are English only. Stay in SPEC scope (no agent runtime, Meal port, Builder Module-package writer, marketplace, Share link, guests). Household Members on one Host are in scope ([ADR 0012](docs/adr/0012-household-members.md)): the Owner adds Members; Members use Bot list and Chat. Settings, Bot create/delete, and Members stay with the Owner. Before commit, run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` when `node_modules` is missing, then `CI=1 pnpm check` (`scripts/ensure-installed.mjs` exits with that install hint when `node_modules/.bin/eslint` is missing). Except pure-markdown commits (`docs/adr/`, CONTEXT, SPEC-only) when the working tree has no app/code changes (a bare `pnpm exec eslint` in an editor or agent session can detect the editor and skip rules; `CI=1` matches GitHub Actions). Unit tests run from the repo root (`pnpm exec vitest run packages/…/tests/unit/….test.ts` or `apps/…`); do not use `pnpm --filter … exec vitest`. New workspace dependencies go in the `pnpm-workspace.yaml` catalog first, then `"catalog:"` in package.json (`pnpm/json-enforce-catalog` fails `CI=1 pnpm check` otherwise). Discard a probe dependency by reverting `package.json` (and `pnpm-lock.yaml` if dirty), then `pnpm install`, not `pnpm remove --lockfile-only`. Create a feature branch with no upstream: `git checkout -b feat/… origin/main` tracks `origin/main`, and a bare `git push` then updates main. Push with `git push -u origin HEAD`. Before editing `AGENTS.md` or `.cursor/rules` from `main`, or before basing a docs or rules change on that tip, run `git fetch origin main` so the tip matches GitHub.
